  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> x1 Base Weapon Cost [Minimum 1,000eb]<br><strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 0 (Weapon Mod)<br><strong>Mods:</strong> All Non-Explosive Weapons which deal damage</p>\n<p>For Non-Explosive weapons that deal damage: +1d6 damage and +1 Autofire rating, including alternate modes such as shotgun shells (edit the weapon's damage and Autofire by hand). The weapon can't be concealed, silenced, or suppressed, and Tech Upgrades can't remove these drawbacks. Existing BODY requirements rise by half (rounded up) the number of damage dice it now rolls on a non-Aimed Single Shot. A weapon with no BODY minimum to wield gains one: that dice count x2, +2 if One-Handed or a bow, +1 if ROF 2+, +2 if Autofire-only or already Autofire 5+. Being mounted also satisfies it. A One-Handed weapon may be made Two-Handed when this is installed. Example: a 3d6, ROF 2, one-handed Heavy Pistol becomes 4d6 and needs BODY 11 (4x2 + 2 + 1), or BODY 9 if made Two-Handed. Autofire-only weapons use their base type's dice for this (Assault Rifle for machine guns) but still can't fire Single Shot.</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Costs the base weapon's cost (minimum 1,000eb); the listed price is the minimum.</li></ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Weapons &gt; Mod Catalog &gt; Weapon Mods).</em></p>"
  },
